    "primary_subject_agency_id": "37330114-0b02-5b61-a889-2fc214849095",
    "summary": "A Skagit County (WA) Superior Court ruled that ALPR images captured by Flock Safety cameras for the cities of Stanwood and Sedro-Woolley are public records under Washington's Public Records Act, rejecting the cities' arguments that data stored on Flock's servers wasn't a public record until accessed. Despite the ruling, requester Jose Rodriguez won't receive the footage because the cities allowed it to auto-delete during litigation. EFF situates the ruling amid broader scrutiny of Flock, including ICE/CBP data sharing and the El Cajon AG lawsuit.",
    "key_quotes": [
      {
        "quote": "The Flock images generated by the Flock cameras...are public records",
        "paragraph_idx": 4
      },
      {
        "quote": "data generated by Flock [automated license plate reader cameras (ALPRs)] and stored in the Flock cloud system are not public records unless and until a public agency extracts and downloads that data.",
        "paragraph_idx": 7
      },
      {
        "quote": "The cities both allowed the records to be automatically deleted after I submitted my records requests and while they decided to have their legal council review my request.",
        "paragraph_idx": 15
      }
    ],
